{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>The light of the righteous rejoices</b> — by way of parable, for when it shines it is as though it rejoices, like \"let him exult as a warrior\" and \"the light of the righteous is like the light of the world to come,\" or the light of salvation, as in: \"light dawns upon them and there shall be radiance.\" Another interpretation: it is possible that the light and the lamp allude to their soul, emanated from the light of HaShem, and he likened the soul of the righteous to the light of the sun that shines, and the soul of the wicked to a lamp, which has no permanence and is consumed. And he said \"rejoices\" as in \"my soul shall exult.\"" "<b>But the lamp of the wicked shall be extinguished</b> — that their soul shall die before its time, and this is correct, as in \"the lamp of Elohim is the soul of man.\""], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:34.510000327Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}